# Cloud of Darkness (3/3 flying): "When Cloud of Darkness enters, target creature an opponent controls gets -X/-X until end of turn, where X is the number of permanent cards
# in your graveyard." Turn 1 Bot1 casts Ancestral Recall (an instant: in its graveyard, but not a permanent card). Turn 2 Bot2 casts Black Lotus and sacrifices it (a permanent card
# in Bot2's graveyard, not Bot1's) and an Ornithopter (0/2). Turn 3 Bot1 sacrifices its own Black Lotus for mana (the one permanent card in its graveyard) and casts Cloud:
# X = 1, so the Ornithopter is -1/1 (X = 2, counting Ancestral Recall or Bot2's Lotus, would kill it); Bot1's own Memnite and Cloud are no targets, so the Ornithopter is the one legal target and is chosen without asking.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
